 "what": "Which run links and which commits named in the result records of results/ exist in the published repository, read on 2026-10-18 with the GitHub API (repos/JacoboPacheco/third-of-a-percent/actions/runs/<id>: a run that exists is 'completed'; repos/.../commits/<sha> and repos/.../compare/<sha>...main: 'ahead' means the commit is an ancestor of main, 'diverged' that it is on another branch). Groups are the result folders without their run id. The ids are every run id named in a results/**/*.json record, in dayone/results and in versions/results. The commits are the repository commits the records name: run.commit, and source.repo_sha in the census records (the other commit fields of the census and of results/lostloops-live-* are commits of the upstream projects they analysed and are not listed). A record of what was read, not a proof; tests/test_readme_numbers.py checks that the ids and commits in the results/ records are the ones listed and that the sentences of README.md and readme-parts/DETAILS.md say exactly this.",
